BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-w1-mon-am-20260511@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260511T053000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260511T070000
SUMMARY:Week 01 — Lower Strength + Sled Development [AM]
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Build lower body strength and Hyrox sled power without excessive fatigue carryover.\n\nWARM-UP 10 min\n- Hip circles x10 each direction\n- Glute bridges 2x15 (2-sec hold at top)\n- Goblet squat 2x10 light (2-sec pause at bottom)\n- Ankle rotations x10 each\n- Banded clamshells 2x15 each side\n\nBACK SQUAT — 4x5 @ RPE 7 (approx 80–87kg)\n  3 min rest. Brace 360 degrees\, knees track toes\, hip crease below knee\, drive floor away. No torso collapse. If bar drifts forward\, reduce load. Log weight and RPE.\n\nROMANIAN DEADLIFT — 4x6 @ RPE 7 (approx 75–85kg)\n  2.5 min rest. Push hips back not down\, neutral spine\, feel hamstrings load before reversing\, bar within 5cm of legs. Log weight and RPE.\n\nWALKING LUNGE — 3x20m @ 40kg\n  2 min rest. Upright torso\, rear knee hovers 2cm from floor\, drive through front heel\, lead knee does not cave.\n\nSLED PUSH — 6x15m moderate load\, 60 sec rest\n  Lean ~45 degrees forward\, short powerful strides\, balls of feet\, full hip extension each step.\n\nSLED PULL — 6x15m moderate load\, 60 sec rest\n  Face away from sled\, drive arms back\, upright posture\, quick short steps\, lean slightly back to keep rope tension.\n\nCORE FINISHER — 3 rounds\, 45 sec rest\n  Plank 60 sec + side plank 30 sec each side + dead bug 10 reps\n\nKPI: No form breakdown. Squat depth consistent. Sled pace steady. Log all working weights.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming session: Lower Strength + Sled Development
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-w1-mon-pm-20260511@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260511T161500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260511T173000
SUMMARY:Week 01 — Run Z2 + Strides [PM]
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Active aerobic maintenance. Reinforce easy running economy with neuromuscular strides.\n\nWARM-UP 10 min\n- 5 min easy jog HR < 135\n- Leg swings x10 each leg\n- High knees 2x20m\, butt kicks 2x20m\, A-skips 2x20m\n\nMAIN SET — 40 min Z2\n  HR cap 135–150 strict. Target pace 5:40–6:10/km flat terrain. HR governs — not pace. Nasal breathing — if you must open your mouth\, you are going too hard. Check posture every 10 min.\n\nSTRIDES — 6x20 sec\n  85% controlled fast — not a sprint. Tall posture\, quick ground contact\, relaxed jaw\, arms drive back without crossing midline. 60 sec walk/jog full recovery between each.\n\nCOOL-DOWN 5 min: Easy jog to walk. 5 deep diaphragmatic breaths.\n\nKPI: Avg HR below 148. No cardiac drift in final 15 min. Log avg HR and avg pace.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming session: Run Z2 + Strides
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-w1-tue-am-20260512@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260512T053000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260512T064500
SUMMARY:Week 01 — Swim Technique + CSS Prep [AM]
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Reinforce technique from Thursday. Introduce more aerobic load.\n\nWARM-UP: 300m easy mixed strokes. No effort. Relaxed neck position.\n\nDRILL SET — 8x50m (25m drill + 25m swim)\, 20 sec rest\n  Rep 1–2: Catch-up drill\n  Rep 3–4: Fingertip drag (enforce high elbow on recovery)\n  Rep 5–6: 6-kick switch (hip rotation)\n  Rep 7–8: weakest drill from earlier\n\nAEROBIC SET — 6x100m\, 20 sec rest. HR below 145.\n  Target 16–18 stroke cycles per 25m (32–36 arm strokes). 2-beat kick — balance only. Exhale fully underwater before rotating to breathe. Head rotation minimal — one goggle in\, one out.\n\nPULL SET — 200m pull buoy easy\n  High elbow catch\, forearm presses back through water\, chest slightly down.\n\nKPI: Breathing every 3 strokes throughout. Relaxed neck and shoulders. Hips not sinking. Stroke count stable or decreasing.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming session: Swim Technique + CSS Prep
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rm-w1-tue-pm-20260512@rippedmechanics
DTSTAMP:20260505T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260512T161500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Copenhagen:20260512T173000
SUMMARY:Week 01 — Bike Threshold [PM]
DESCRIPTION:PURPOSE: Second threshold stimulus of the week. Establish FTP repeatability.\nFUEL: 40–60g fast carbs 20 min before. 500ml water during.\n\nWARM-UP 15 min\n- Progressive build 100W to 170W\n- Cadence 90–95 rpm\n- 3x20 sec fast-pedal at 110+ rpm (at min 8\, 10\, 12)\n\nMAIN SET — 3x10 min @ 218–230W (95–100% FTP)\, 5 min easy spin 120–140W between\n  Interval 1: Start 218W. Let HR settle by min 2 (expect 168–172). Target HR 170–174 by min 5. Do not exceed 178.\n  Interval 2: If interval 1 finished below HR 175\, target 222–225W. Otherwise hold 218W.\n  Interval 3: Hard cap HR 180. Cadence above 88 rpm. If power must drop to hold HR\, accept it.\n\nCOOL-DOWN 10 min: Easy spin 160W down to 90W.\n\nKPI: Power CV below 5% per interval. HR below 180 throughout. RPE 7–8 in final minute. Log avg power and avg HR per interval.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT90M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming session: Bike Threshold
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT

END:VCALENDAR
